  [0;36mResponse:[0m This is a classic riddle or trick question!

The key is understanding **how drying works on a clothesline**.

If 4 towels take 4 hours to dry in the sun, that implies that **each towel dries independently**, assuming they’re all exposed to the same sunlight and airflow.

So, whether you have 4 towels or 20 towels, **each towel still needs 4 hours to dry**, *as long as*:

- They’re all spread out and not overlapping (so each gets equal sun/air),
- The clothesline is long enough to hold them all without crowding,
- Weather conditions (sun intensity, humidity, wind) remain the same.

✅ Therefore, **20 towels also take 4 hours to dry**, under the same conditions.

> 🌞 **Answer: 4 hours**

*(This assumes ideal drying conditions where drying time per towel is independent of the number of other towels — which is usually the intended interpretation of this riddle.)*
